Let me check: how does TQue work?

TQue is a queue of LocalTensor. When you call AllocTensor, it allocates a new LocalTensor from the queue's memory. When you call FreeTensor, it frees the memory back to the queue.

So the pattern should be:
```cpp
for each tile:
    // Get input
    LocalTensor<T> xTyped = inQueue.AllocTensor<T>();
    DataCopy(xTyped, xGm[offset], valid);
    inQueue.EnQue(xTyped);
    LocalTensor<T> xIn = inQueue.DeQue<T>();

    // Compute
    Cast(xFp32Buf, xIn, CAST_NONE, valid);
    // ... compute ...

    // Put output
    LocalTensor<T> yTyped = outQueue.AllocTensor<T>();
    Cast(yTyped, yFp32Buf, CAST_ROUND, valid);
    outQueue.EnQue(yTyped);
    LocalTensor<T> yOut = outQueue.DeQue<T>();
    DataCopy(yGm[offset], yOut, valid);

    // Free
    inQueue.FreeTensor(xIn);
    outQueue.FreeTensor(yOut);
```

This way, the buffers are properly managed.

